-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- selection by content
-- A piece of a document kept whole (a file the source holds as it is, such as docs/Hyperactive_Labs.md)
-- selects by content (2026-11-17): the paragraphs beginning at the first line that begins with a given
-- text. No edit elsewhere moves it; an edit of its first line is seen at once, since it then selects
-- another paragraph or none. A piece's lines are always a run of the document's own lines
-- (paragraphs-split, prefix-split).
-- the lines of a text, split at its newlines
text-lines-add : Word → List (List Word) → List (List Word)
text-lines-add x nil = cons (cons x nil) nil
text-lines-add x (cons l ls) = cons (cons x l) ls
